Figure \ref{Fig:Figure-Px} displays $P(x)$ for the reaction between carbon monoxide and water, starting with a 0.1M concentration of \ce{CO} and a 0.2 M concentration of \ce{H2O}. The equilibrium constant for this reaction at 527 $^\circ$C is 4. We can see that the polynomial is a parabola with two roots $ x_1$=0.08 M and $ x_2$=0.3 M. Only the first root would represent the extent of the reaction $x$ as we cannot prodice 0.3M from either 0.1M or 0.2M. Therefore, only $ x_1$=0.08 M has chemical sense.












